WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.080
<v The Heroine>Hi. Welcome to LAiDIES. Before the
season starts, I owe you a tour.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:11.475
<v The Heroine>This is a show about learning AI — made
for women who are already smart, already

00:00:11.475 --> 00:00:15.060
<v The Heroine>busy, and not remotely interested in a
forty-hour course.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:21.220
<v The Heroine>It works like the TV we grew up on:
twenty-four episode seasons, a new one
every Wednesday.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:25.935
<v The Heroine>Each episode is shorter than your
commute, and each one gives you exactly

00:00:25.935 --> 00:00:29.915
<v The Heroine>one useful thing — explained the way
your sharpest girlfriend would explain

00:00:29.915 --> 00:00:34.680
<v The Heroine>it over coffee, with the pop culture you
were raised on and none of the jargon
you weren't.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:41.980
<v The Heroine>I'm your heroine. I can't say that with
a straight face either, but the promo
guy insists.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:46.760
<v The Heroine>I'm not an expert — I'm a few steps
ahead of you, that's all.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:52.601
<v The Heroine>I put off learning AI for longer than
I'll admit on the record — the full

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:59.360
<v The Heroine>confession is Episode One — and now I'm
walking the road one Wednesday at a time
and reporting back.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.800
<v The Heroine>I make the mistakes so you can skip
them.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:05.560
<v The Heroine>I do the reading so you don't have to.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:10.820
<v The Heroine>So what can you expect in season one?
Remember the promo guy?

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:14.980
<v The Heroine>He's been pacing the booth, dying to do
his big voice.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.480
<v The Heroine>So I'll let him set up the season, and
I'll meet you on the other side for the
actual tour.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:22.200
<v The Heroine>Take it away.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:26.460
<v The Announcer>On this season of LAiDIES: she stops
feeling behind.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:31.320
<v The Announcer>She learns to delegate to machines —
without lowering her standards.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:34.580
<v The Announcer>She builds her own little squad of AI
helpers.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:39.100
<v The Announcer>And she becomes the woman other people
come to when the future gets confusing.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:41.380
<v The Announcer>But first... the tour.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.060
<v The Announcer>This is the trailer: Welcome to
SUNNYVAiLE.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:46.180
<v The Heroine>So — SUNNYVAiLE.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:54.660
<v The Heroine>The 90s had Sunnydale, Bayside, and
Capeside. Silicon Valley has SUNNYVAiLE.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:56.920
<v The Heroine>You have sunnyVEIL.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:05.040
<v The Heroine>That's Sunny v-A-I-l-e. See what we did
there?

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:10.583
<v The Heroine>When I finally started learning this
stuff, everything about AI looked like a

00:02:10.583 --> 00:02:12.680
<v The Heroine>stock photo of a glowing blue brain.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:17.240
<v The Heroine>And I refused to spend a year of
Wednesdays somewhere that ugly.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:22.837
<v The Heroine>So we built a town instead — set
somewhere around nineteen ninety-nine,

00:02:22.837 --> 00:02:26.060
<v The Heroine>and furnished with the entire era that
raised us.

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.600
<v The Heroine>Call it nineteen ninety to twenty ten.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:33.500
<v The Heroine>Boy bands and girl groups. Sleepover
games.

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:35.620
<v The Heroine>Hair full of butterfly clips.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:41.040
<v The Heroine>Calling in to the radio station to
request a song so you could record it on
cassette.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:46.390
<v The Heroine>The glory days of twenty-four-episode
seasons, back when they let you fall in

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:49.360
<v The Heroine>love with the characters before
cancelling everything.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:56.480
<v The Heroine>That era wired us — and it turns out it
wired us perfectly for this.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:04.560
<v The Heroine>Because SUNNYVAiLE is where Girl power
meets machine power. Analogies that
stick.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:10.680
<v The Heroine>In a fictional town from an era we know
and love. That's how we're teaching it.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.560
<v The Heroine>Ladies is the show, SUNNYVAiLE is where
every episode takes place.

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:17.920
<v The Heroine>And I live here — actually live here.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:22.700
<v The Heroine>I found this place at eleven p.m. on a
Tuesday, looking for something else.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:29.928
<v The Heroine>Most residents do. My card's in my
wallet, my closet's upstairs at the
sorority house, and the

00:03:29.928 --> 00:03:34.927
<v The Heroine>story you'll hear this season happens in
these streets: the late-night research

00:03:34.927 --> 00:03:39.300
<v The Heroine>at the library, the coffee at my corner
table, the songs on the radio.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.940
<v The Heroine>Every building is a page.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.280
<v The Heroine>Walking in is just clicking.

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:48.720
<v The Heroine>And the town remembers your visits —
hold that thought.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:53.710
<v The Heroine>But here's what I actually need you to
hear, because at first glance it looks

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:55.580
<v The Heroine>like we just built something cute.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.040
<v The Heroine>The town IS the teaching method.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.300
<v The Heroine>Every episode teaches one concept.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:04.420
<v The Heroine>The study pack reinforces it.

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:07.860
<v The Heroine>The song turns it into an earworm you
can't shake.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:09.960
<v The Heroine>The pop quiz tests it.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.260
<v The Heroine>The games make you practice it.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:14.840
<v The Heroine>The community pressure-checks it.

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:21.089
<v The Heroine>Every part of town echoes every other
part, on purpose — because when you're

00:04:21.089 --> 00:04:24.180
<v The Heroine>busy, that echo is what makes learning
stick.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:31.400
<v The Heroine>We think in analogies and stories;
that's not a weakness, it's how AI
finally makes sense.

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:35.840
<v The Heroine>We built a world because worlds work.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:40.877
<v The Heroine>And one more thing before the walking
starts — I keep saying

00:04:40.877 --> 00:04:46.611
<v The Heroine>Wednesday...because on wednesdays we do
AI (obviously), but let me tell you what

00:04:46.611 --> 00:04:48.380
<v The Heroine>Wednesday actually means.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:54.845
<v The Heroine>A new episode drops every Wednesday, and
the town dresses for it: new anthem on

00:04:54.845 --> 00:04:59.837
<v The Heroine>the radio, new study pack at the coffee
shop, new charms hidden around

00:04:59.837 --> 00:05:05.392
<v The Heroine>town...(we might even wear pink!) But
the town itself is open every day of the

00:05:05.392 --> 00:05:07.220
<v The Heroine>week, and nothing expires.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:14.600
<v The Heroine>You can visit any building and do any
activity in any order, on its own,
whenever you want.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:18.680
<v The Heroine>Start today. Start next month.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:25.663
<v The Heroine>Go back to episode one — the tapes stay
on the shelf at the rental store forever

00:05:25.663 --> 00:05:32.140
<v The Heroine>— catch up at your own pace, binge a
little if you're behind, or slow down
and sit with one.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:39.226
<v The Heroine>Come back anytime for a re-read, a
re-watch, a re-listen, or to have fun

00:05:39.226 --> 00:05:41.180
<v The Heroine>with one of the activities.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:45.040
<v The Heroine>Wednesday is when the new thing arrives.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:47.760
<v The Heroine>Every other day is yours.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:53.356
<v The Heroine>But if you want to get the most out of
SUNNYVAiLE, do one of the weekly tours

00:05:53.356 --> 00:05:55.000
<v The Heroine>so the learning really sticks.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:59.400
<v The Heroine>You might even meet some new friends
along the way. Now.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:03.300
<v The Heroine>There are two types of tours in
SUNNYVAiLE and both count.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:10.500
<v The Heroine>The Express Tour is four stops: the
week's episode; the study pack, the
quiz, and the song.

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:16.561
<v The Heroine>The Full Tour is the loop — eight stops
through town, all tracked by your Tour

00:06:16.561 --> 00:06:20.660
<v The Heroine>Guide who ticks each stop automatically
the moment you show up.

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:26.120
<v The Heroine>Finish all eight before next Wednesday
and you bank an extra wish with the
Fairy Godmother.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:31.440
<v The Heroine>I'll introduce her in a minute. It's the
nineties. Just go with it.

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:34.860
<v The Heroine>Here's the Full Tour, in walking order.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:39.100
<v The Heroine>Stop one: the NewsStand — first door on
Main Street.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:45.778
<v The Heroine>The week's AI headlines, translated into
actual English: what happened, why it

00:06:45.778 --> 00:06:48.500
<v The Heroine>matters to your job, no doom, no hype.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:51.740
<v The Heroine>Plus the bigger themes we are tracking
in AI.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:54.960
<v The Heroine>Five minutes, and you're the informed
one in the meeting.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:59.680
<v The Heroine>Stop two: the Chick Flicks, our video
rental store.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:06.800
<v The Heroine>Every episode lives here like a tape on
a shelf, sorted into genre aisles you
can actually browse.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:11.991
<v The Heroine>Grab this week's — and if you want the
full experience, there's a screening

00:07:11.991 --> 00:07:16.720
<v The Heroine>room in the back where episodes play
with the pictures — the premiere is
screening now.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.780
<v The Heroine>It's where you'd take a friend for her
first one.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:25.712
<v The Heroine>Stop three: the Blend and Snap — the
coffee shop, and third on the loop

00:07:25.712 --> 00:07:28.340
<v The Heroine>because by now you'll want to sit down.

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:33.819
<v The Heroine>This is where the week's study pack
lives: the class notes — a cheat sheet

00:07:33.819 --> 00:07:39.620
<v The Heroine>of what the episode taught and what to
remember for the quiz — plus this week's
trading card pack.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:43.320
<v The Heroine>Rip it open, flip each card, learn a
concept.

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:47.660
<v The Heroine>Old packs stay on the back shelf, so you
can always catch up.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:50.780
<v The Heroine>I write half this show from the corner
table.

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:57.134
<v The Heroine>The pack also hands you the try-on: each
week's ten-minute exercise, where you

00:07:57.134 --> 00:08:01.360
<v The Heroine>try the lesson on one small, real task
from your actual life.

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:06.080
<v The Heroine>If you only do one thing beyond
listening, do the try-on.

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:08.380
<v The Heroine>It's why the pack exists.

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:12.700
<v The Heroine>Stop four: SUNNYVAiLE High, up
Schoolhouse Road.

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:18.282
<v The Heroine>The pop quiz — ten questions on the
episode, plus 2 bonus questions, a

00:08:18.282 --> 00:08:23.220
<v The Heroine>couple of minutes, and your score banks
butterfly clips in a jar in your closet.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.620
<v The Heroine>Best score counts, so you can always
retake.

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:34.200
<v The Heroine>And every four weeks, the gym hosts a
book fair. Yes, that kind. Yes, with
posters.

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:39.980
<v The Heroine>Stop five is scheduled free time — my
favourite kind of structure.

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:42.500
<v The Heroine>This is when the town shows off.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:48.132
<v The Heroine>Get your cards read at Madame Cleo's;
she does walk-ins, and she will tell you

00:08:48.132 --> 00:08:50.380
<v The Heroine>the read, the message, and the move.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:53.280
<v The Heroine>Her fortunes do NOT disappoint!

00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:56.580
<v The Heroine>I go more often than I'm prepared to
admit.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:00.160
<v The Heroine>Pick up the Dream Phone and call
somebody in nineteen ninety-nine.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:07.803
<v The Heroine>Ask the Fairy Godmother anything — she's
the town's actual AI assistant, a real

00:09:07.803 --> 00:09:11.200
<v The Heroine>one: bring the question, she brings the
answer.

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:17.360
<v The Heroine>And yes, that wish you banked for
finishing the Full Tour? Spent with her.

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:23.420
<v The Heroine>Or go hunting: every week, seven charms
hide in pictures around town.

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:28.500
<v The Heroine>Spot one, click it, and it's added to
your charm bracelet in your closet.

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:31.920
<v The Heroine>Stop six: Makeover on Main.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:37.040
<v The Heroine>This is where you get your SUNNYVAiLE
glow up.... your residence card.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:42.240
<v The Heroine>The town's version of a membership, and
the two most useful minutes on the tour.

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:49.805
<v The Heroine>It's free. You pick a handle, and from
then on the town remembers you: quiz
clips, charms,

00:09:49.805 --> 00:09:53.480
<v The Heroine>stickers, wishes, tour progress —
everything banks.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:58.140
<v The Heroine>Without a card you're a tourist; things
happen, but nothing sticks.

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:00.580
<v The Heroine>With one, you're a resident.

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:05.417
<v The Heroine>And you can come back any week to
freshen the card after you've completed

00:10:05.417 --> 00:10:09.820
<v The Heroine>the week— your favourite saint, your
favourite cocktail, your favourite
quote.

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:13.920
<v The Heroine>Stop seven: the Bronze Age. Happy hour.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:19.213
<v The Heroine>The bar serves the Businesswomen's
Special — a paper fortune teller, the

00:10:19.213 --> 00:10:22.700
<v The Heroine>kind you folded in fifth grade, picks
your drink of the week.

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:27.743
<v The Heroine>This is your reminder to book that
overdue happy hour with the girls— and

00:10:27.743 --> 00:10:31.660
<v The Heroine>we even have tools to help make
scheduling and meeting easy and fun.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:38.100
<v The Heroine>And stop eight: the sorority house —
Delta Lai Nu, on Wisteria Lane.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:44.600
<v The Heroine>The rooms live here — our members-only
chat, a full hallway of them in three
wings.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:50.580
<v The Heroine>Common rooms, where you post your wins
and we cheer, or ask the house anything.

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:53.580
<v The Heroine>Advice rooms, like Dear Ladies.

00:10:54.540 --> 00:11:00.037
<v The Heroine>Creative rooms, where mix CDs get traded
and the Burn Book collects what didn't

00:11:00.037 --> 00:11:03.060
<v The Heroine>work — we keep receipts on our own
mistakes.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:09.580
<v The Heroine>And the feature of the house: Girl Talk,
where you draw a card and take the dare.

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:14.980
<v The Heroine>This is also where the weekly sign-off
challenge lands. And upstairs?

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:21.520
<v The Heroine>Your closet — the room where everything
you've collected is on display. Your
card.

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:24.800
<v The Heroine>Your clips. Your charms. Your
luminaries.

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:28.780
<v The Heroine>End the loop there, and admire the shelf
you're building.

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:31.180
<v The Heroine>Now — the radio.

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:36.167
<v The Heroine>I saved it because it's my favourite
building in town, and because it is not

00:11:36.167 --> 00:11:38.060
<v The Heroine>just where the episode songs live.

00:11:39.620 --> 00:11:45.095
<v The Heroine>K-S-V-L, community radio, ninety-nine
point nine, at the end of Main Street —

00:11:45.095 --> 00:11:47.060
<v The Heroine>a full, functioning station.

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:53.169
<v The Heroine>Turn on the live rotation and you get DJ
SunnyV between tracks, station jingles,

00:11:53.169 --> 00:11:58.140
<v The Heroine>weather and traffic reports for a town
that has neither weather nor traffic,

00:11:58.140 --> 00:12:01.820
<v The Heroine>and commercials for the storefronts you
just walked past.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:08.737
<v The Heroine>The music is real and it's ours: ten
house bands — every name is an AI joke

00:12:08.737 --> 00:12:14.474
<v The Heroine>you'll start catching around episode six
— plus a new anthem every episode,

00:12:14.474 --> 00:12:17.720
<v The Heroine>because every lesson here has its own
song.

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:22.880
<v The Heroine>There are mix CDs you can flip over and
read like it's your best friend's
handwriting.

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:26.300
<v The Heroine>There's a sticker rack, and your first
one's free.

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:33.376
<v The Heroine>The station has one belief, and honestly
it's the town's pedagogy in six words:

00:12:33.376 --> 00:12:37.200
<v The Heroine>don't just learn from books. Learn from
hooks.

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:42.240
<v The Heroine>Turn it on when you arrive — it follows
you from building to building.

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:45.960
<v The Heroine>And there's still more I'm leaving for
you to find.

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:52.914
<v The Heroine>The post office writes you one letter a
week — the episode, the pack, the quiz,

00:12:52.914 --> 00:12:58.589
<v The Heroine>the news, and the song, all in one
envelope — and it ships gifts too: send

00:12:58.589 --> 00:13:02.600
<v The Heroine>a note, a charm, or a saint card to a
friend in town.

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:05.560
<v The Heroine>The mall sells flair for your card.

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:11.780
<v The Heroine>Town Hall is run by Mayor Deb — and Deb
deserves a proper introduction.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:17.341
<v The Heroine>Deb worked at the post office until
nineteen ninety-nine, when her coworkers

00:13:17.341 --> 00:13:23.660
<v The Heroine>put her name on the mayoral ballot as a
joke. She won. She keeps winning.

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:31.320
<v The Heroine>Nobody is more surprised than Deb, who
also happens to be our Patron Saint of
Loop Me Out.

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:35.620
<v The Heroine>Her campaign posters alone are worth the
trip to Town Hall.

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:42.099
<v The Heroine>And up on Lantern Hill, the Luminairy
hangs portraits of the women (and one

00:13:42.099 --> 00:13:47.747
<v The Heroine>rose) in three wings: the patron saints
from the era that raised us, teaching us

00:13:47.747 --> 00:13:52.837
<v The Heroine>the lessons of today, the real-life
mavens who built and questioned this

00:13:52.837 --> 00:13:58.940
<v The Heroine>field, and the trailblazers shipping the
frontier right now. Take the walk.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.560
<v The Heroine>The town rewards snooping.

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:03.960
<v The Heroine>You'll have favourites by Friday.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:08.020
<v The Heroine>Everything I just described lives at
laidies.ai.

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:14.320
<v The Heroine>That's "LAiDIES" spelled with an i in
the middle: L, A, i, D, I, E, S.

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:16.740
<v The Heroine>New episode every Wednesday.

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:22.432
<v The Heroine>Express when you're slammed, Full Tour
when you've got the hour, any day of the

00:14:22.432 --> 00:14:23.840
<v The Heroine>week that works for you.

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:30.120
<v The Heroine>Do it all at once, or one stop at a
time. That's the town. That's the show.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:36.280
<v The Heroine>That's the deal. So remember, LAiDIES:
you don't have to know anything yet.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:39.100
<v The Heroine>You just have to show up.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:42.640
<v The Heroine>See you next Wednesday... in SUNNYVAiLE.

00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:46.480
<v The Heroine>And now back to our promo guy...

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:53.943
<v The Announcer>And on the next episode of LAiDIES: a
man named Steve is called a visionary...

00:14:53.943 --> 00:14:57.420
<v The Announcer>and our heroine finally stops putting it
off.

00:14:58.240 --> 00:15:02.760
<v The Announcer>Tune in next week for Episode One: On
Wednesdays We Use AI.

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:13.780
<v The LAiDIES>Ooh... SUNNYVAiLE.

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:22.340
<v The LAiDIES>You nod in the meeting like you read the thing,

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:27.000
<v The LAiDIES>but you're winging it hard every time the words AI ring.

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:30.820
<v The LAiDIES>They buried it in buzzwords, made it sound so tall—

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:32.860
<v The LAiDIES>honey, you've broken ceilings.

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:43.140
<v The LAiDIES>You just needed a room that moves as smart and as fast.

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:47.040
<v The LAiDIES>So come on... welcome to SUNNYVAiLE.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:53.140
<v The LAiDIES>You're not behind, you're home!
A hundred clever women, and you're never on your own!

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:56.640
<v The LAiDIES>The 90s shaped us—and AI's shaping now.

00:15:56.980 --> 00:16:00.360
<v The LAiDIES>You don't chase the future here, we'll show you how!

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:05.140
<v The LAiDIES>Oh, SUNNYVAiLE... your people are here.
